syndrome that occurs when there is a sudden decline in the glomerular filtration rate. The purpose of this review is to 
examine new developments and clinical applications of renal replacement therapies including hemodialysis, continuous 
renal replacement therapy, the bioartificial kidney, and peritoneal dialysis in the management of this complicated 
